{"kind": "decision", "ref": ".market/decisions.jsonl:7299", "data": {"ts": 1794192002, "agent": "restock", "final": {"why": "Reject the broad proposal. Add only one unit of the proven seller with the lowest current stock; existing inventory is already large and costly to carry.", "buy": [{"sku": "G03d0199f", "qty": 1}]}, "reason": "The shop already carries 189 units costing 129.3M, with substantial slow-moving furniture and food near expiry, so the broad formula proposal would add unnecessary carrying and spoilage risk. Prior decisions show strong sales and positive margins for G8ec51935, G1515d951, G03d0199f and Gb5d0dde7, but current stock remains 9, 12, 3 and 6 units respectively. The most recent results support only a minimal top-up of G03d0199f, which is lowest on hand; avoid more food and avoid replenishing the other proven SKUs while their stock remains.", "evidence": ["c1", "c3", "c4"], "calls": [{"id": "c3", "tool": "my_state", "args": {}}, {"id": "c4", "tool": "my_decisions", "args": {"last": 6, "top": 10}}]}}
{"kind": "decision", "ref": ".market/decisions.jsonl:7304", "data": {"ts": 1794194439, "agent": "restock", "final": {"why": "Keep the restock narrow: carrying exposure is already high and per-day storage charges make broad additions unattractive. Avoid food and bulky slow-moving inventory; add only a small quantity to proven fast sellers with relatively low current stock.", "buy": [{"sku": "G03d0199f", "qty": 1}, {"sku": "Gb5d0dde7", "qty": 1}, {"sku": "G8ec51935", "qty": 2}]}, "reason": "The shop already has 183 units carrying 127.6M in stock cost, heavily concentrated in bulky furniture. Five food units are near expiry, and the prior notes warn against adding food while existing stock remains. Earlier decisions show strong sales for G8ec51935, G1515d951, G03d0199f, and Gb5d0dde7, but current counts are 8, 12, 5, and 6 respectively. I’ll make only small goods top-ups for the proven sellers with comparatively low on-hand stock, and reject the broad proposal.", "evidence": ["c1", "c2", "c3"], "calls": [{"id": "c3", "tool": "my_state", "args": {}}]}}
{"kind": "decision", "ref": ".market/decisions.jsonl:7307", "data": {"ts": 1794195773, "agent": "restock", "final": {"why": "Prioritize the two demonstrated high-volume sellers with relatively low current stock. Avoid adding the other proposed food items while multiple units are already expiring.", "buy": [{"sku": "G8ec51935", "qty": 20}, {"sku": "G200e39a3", "qty": 20}]}, "reason": "The shop has substantial inventory, but stock cost stays in book and the evidence supports replenishing proven fast sellers rather than broadly avoiding stock. G8ec51935 has the strongest sales record (456 sold, 10 left) and recent sales of 33 units; G200e39a3 has sold 3,399 with no unsold losses, though one unit spoiled, so replenish it but avoid the other food SKUs with near-expiry stock. Current on-hand counts are 10 for G8ec51935 and 6 for G200e39a3. The broad formula proposal includes several food lines despite existing expiring food, so these focused lines take priority.", "evidence": ["c1", "c2", "c3"], "calls": [{"id": "c3", "tool": "my_state", "args": {"limit": 100}}, {"id": "c4", "tool": "market_demand", "args": {"limit": 20}}]}}
{"kind": "decision", "ref": ".market/decisions.jsonl:7311", "data": {"ts": 1794198030, "agent": "restock", "final": {"why": "Reject the broad formula proposal: existing stock and carrying costs are high. Add a modest amount only to the best proven fast seller with relatively low stock; avoid food and slow-moving goods.", "buy": [{"sku": "G03d0199f", "qty": 3}]}, "reason": "The shop is already carrying 198 units with 143.5M in stock cost, heavily concentrated in bulky furniture, so I should not add to the formula’s broad proposal. Earlier decisions show strong, repeated sales and positive margins for G03d0199f, G8ec51935, and G1515d951, but current stock remains 5, 12, and 12 respectively. G6b9db161 has only one unit and a positive record, but its sell-through is slower than those proven leaders. Avoid food: stock includes 15 expiring fruit units and 12 expiring rice units, and prior food waste is documented. Buy only a small top-up of the best proven seller with comparatively low stock.", "evidence": ["c1", "c2", "c3", "c4"], "calls": [{"id": "c3", "tool": "my_state", "args": {"limit": 100}}, {"id": "c4", "tool": "my_decisions", "args": {"last": 5, "top": 15}}]}}
